   "claims": [
    "The daily caloric need is the BMR value multiplied by a factor with a value between 1.2 and 1.9, depending on activity level.",
    "It was revised in 1984 to be more accurate and was used up until 1990, when the Mifflin-St Jeor Equation was introduced.",
    "BMR increases approximately 7% for every increase of 1.36 degrees Fahrenheit in the body's internal temperature.",
    "On the other hand, starvation can reduce BMR by as much as 30%.",
    "Modern Wisdom A 2005 meta-analysis study on BMR* showed that when controlling all factors of metabolic rate, there is still a 26% unknown variance between people."
   ],
